## Array

- `push(item)` — adds an item to the end of an array.
- `pop()` — removes the last item from an array.
- `shift()` — removes the first item from an array.
- `unshift(item)` — adds an item to the start of an array.
- `forEach(fn)` — runs a function for every array item.
- `map(fn)` — creates a new array by transforming each item.
- `filter(fn)` — creates a new array with only items that pass a test.
- `find(fn)` — returns the first item that matches a test.
- `includes(value)` — checks if an array contains a value (true/false).
- `join(separator)` — turns an array into a string.
- `sort()` — sorts the array (changes the original array).
- `reduce(fn, start)` — reduces an array to one single value.

## Number / Math

- `Number(value)` — converts something into a number.
- `parseInt(text)` — converts text to an integer number.
- `parseFloat(text)` — converts text to a decimal number.
- `Math.round(n)` — rounds to the nearest integer.
- `Math.floor(n)` — rounds down.
- `Math.ceil(n)` — rounds up.
- `Math.random()` — gives a random number from 0 to 1.

## Object / JSON

- `Object.keys(obj)` — gets all keys of an object as an array.
- `Object.values(obj)` — gets all values of an object as an array.
- `Object.entries(obj)` — gets key/value pairs as an array.
- `JSON.stringify(obj)` — converts an object to a JSON string.
- `JSON.parse(text)` — converts a JSON string to an object.

## DOM (very common)

- `document.getElementById(id)` — selects an element by its id.
- `document.querySelector(css)` — selects the first element matching CSS selector.
- `document.querySelectorAll(css)` — selects all matching elements (NodeList).
- `addEventListener(event, fn)` — runs code when an event happens (like click).
- `classList.add(name)` — adds a CSS class to an element.
- `classList.remove(name)` — removes a CSS class from an element.
- `classList.toggle(name)` — adds/removes a class depending on current state.